  "findings": [
    "SequenceSelfArrow now shares one width/start/segment-length value for legacy forward self constraints, group bounds, right extent and paint. Java MessageSelfArrow preferred width adds live-segment length, and ConstraintAfter adds it again. Account precedes implementation and replaced created/destroyed padding constants were removed.",
    "The new value omits Java isReverse: MessageSelfArrow#getStartingX returns pos2-preferredWidth for reverse definition, while SequenceSelfArrow always uses right+activation_delta. Focused reversed async controls at depths0 and2 fail with a missing left envelope. This is a direction dependency of the shared geometry, not a reason to carve away failed inputs.",
    "All eight own primary padded attached-note/newpage cases fail. In the legacy case the attached note starts y97.2988 in Rust versus91.2988 in Java at padding3; the first-page loop itself can agree while the whole component does not. Later-page horizontal handling removes crashes but does not prove all-page composition. The envelope remains dependent on NoteBox/ArrowAndNoteBox and page composition repairs.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
